  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammed Saeed Khan S/O Nisar Ahmed Khan vs State Of Maharashtra on 29 August, 2022 Author: Bharati Dangre Bench: Bharati Dangre 1/3 16 ABA-2175-22.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.2175 Of 2022 Mohammed Saeed Khan s/o Nisar .. Applicant Ahmed Khan Versus The State of Maharashtra .. Respondent ... Mr.Ashok Kumar Dubey with Mr.Abhinav Duney and Ms.Shweta R. Yadav i/b Savj Law Solutions for the Applicant. Ms.Anamika Malhotra, A.P.P. for the State/Respondent. Psi Dighe, attached to L.T.Marg Police Station, present. ... Coram: Bharati Dangre, J. Dated : 29th August, 2022 P.C:- 1. The present applicant apprehend his arrest i C.R.No.658 of 2022 registered with L.T.Marg Police Station for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 179, 272, 273 of Ipc and Sections 26(2), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(c), 3 and 59 of the Foods Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 2. The subject C.R. arraigns one Shaf Shamshul Aalam as an accused, who was intercepted and found in possession of prohibited substance in form of pan masala and gutka, which Mohammed Saeed Khan S/O Nisar Ahmed Khan vs State Of Maharashtra on 29 August, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/16428496/ 1 M.M.Salgaonkar ::: Uploaded on - 30/08/2022 ::: Downloaded on - 30/08/202 2/3 16 ABA-2175-22.doc was seized by the police.",
    "facts": "The said substance was worth Rs.3,83,960/-. In his remand report, name of the present applicant has surfaced as a 'supplier' to him. 3. Pertinent to note that said Shaf Shamshul Aalam was arrested and was released on bail on 14/06/2022 by the learned Magistrate, Mazgaon. Considering the legal position revolving around invocation of Section 328 of IPC and since the legal conundrum is pending before the highest Court of this country, the applicant deserves his protection from arrest by way of following ad-interim order.",
